From 58bcd6e706f771d699205fb4aebce8f0aa1c0919 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:21:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 42/49] fixup! v2: swap CBlockHeader and block index to
 134-byte V2 header and BLAKE3 BlockId

A backward reorg missed every parent in the64-slot native state cache because disk reconstruction retained only its requested tip. The next parent replayed all deltas from genesis again under cs_main, starving block serving until peers hit their120s download timeout. Retain only the nearest64 reconstructed ancestors through the existing bounded LRU and mark them persisted because their complete files were read. Preserve64-entry limits and atomic persistence failure; no timeout, consensus or rejection changes.

The unchanged original four-node4110/4112-block reorg functional fails before320.5s and passes after32.61s. Full candidate-state suite, including failed eviction/import and strict root checks, passes0.98s.

Tier: V2 (fixup to v2: swap CBlockHeader and block index to134-byte V2 header and BLAKE3 BlockId)
---
 src/primitives/block.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/primitives/block.cpp b/src/primitives/block.cpp
index e10edda338..d8de813b78 100644
--- a/src/primitives/block.cpp
+++ b/src/primitives/block.cpp
@@ -491,11 +491,18 @@ bool LoadV2BlockStateFromDiskLocked(std::unique_lock<std::mutex> &lock, const Bl
         built.inserted_coins = std::move(it->inserted_coins);
         built.circulating_supply =
             running_root ? running_root->total_value : 0;
+        // These states came from complete files, so their cache eviction does
+        // not need to rewrite them. Keep only the nearest bounded window: a
+        // deep rewind can then reuse its reconstructed parents instead of
+        // replaying the whole delta history again for every disconnected tip.
+        built.persisted_to_disk = true;
         if (it + 1 == chain.rend()) {
             snap = built;
         }
-        // Reconstructed ancestors are owned locally; only the requested state
-        // is offered to the bounded cache by the caller.
+        if (static_cast<size_t>(chain.rend() - it) <= kMaxCachedV2StateSnapshots &&
+            !CacheV2BlockStateLocked(lock, it->block_hash, std::move(built))) {
+            throw V2StateCacheError("Unable to cache reconstructed V2 state");
+        }
     }
     return true;
 }
